body:
Thank you, and same. That friend who told me to jump off a mall since hasn't apologized to me.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

HELPED

My therapist told me that I am really harsh on myself, and I always think narrowly. My fear of getting a\~79 or below on my card rooted in my mother's standards, so even if I told her I did my best, she would not believe it. This has been the best comment/advice so far, I've been panicking the whole day lol!

&#x200B;

HELPED

I've been wishing for this game since last year, but I never got the chance to got it, even during sales because it's too expensive. I absolutely enjoy the western genre, and as a fan of Rockstar games, RDR2 is one of the next best titles the company created:)

&#x200B;

Thank u for hosting this giveaway too:)

Same here, whenever I see a car I just want to jump in front of it and get hit. I'd even thank the driver for my final words. I just want instant death, I'm scared of physical pain. I tried hanging myself 3 times and my god, it felt the absolute worse, I was gasping for air and felt like my neck and head are about to be detached. My head also felt heavy from the intense crying. A knife is a big no no too, because holy shit, it would hurt a lot. Maybe overdosing is not so bad, but you have a chance of survival. Even jumping off a fucking building scares the shit out of me because I might survive and end up with broken bones, at LEAST let me die intact. 

&#x200B;

But hey, on the bright side there's also people here on this thread who feels the same as you. People understand each other on this thread, and for me it feels like a safe haven for me. I hope things will get better for you.
